<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - CBOT gains shut off demand.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - CBOT gains shut off demand.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sharp gains in CBOT soymeal futures Tuesday shut off demand for rail and truck soymeal, and basis offers were unchanged as a result, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There aren't going to be any buyers at these levels,&quot; said one southeastern broker. &quot;It's also got to be killing the export demand.&quot;</p>
<p>CBOT March soymeal futures soared as much as $4.80 per ton in early trade, lifted mostly by double-digit gains in soybean futures, traders said.</p>
<p>One Indiana dealer said his soymeal supplies would remain tight through the week because of maintenance downtime.</p>
<p>&quot;We're supposed to be down for about 24 hours this week, so that should keep things tight,&quot; the dealer said.  </p>
